{"id":"mahabharata-9-003","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":3,"title":"तृतीयोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 3 · Sanjaya tells of the Kuru loss","summary":{"en":"Sanjaya tells how, with Karna slain, Kripa lamented and the Kauravas, grieving, gathered around Duryodhana. Kripa advises that the army cannot go on without a leader.","kn":"ಕರ್ಣ ಹತನಾದ ಮೇಲೆ ಕೃಪ ವಿಲಪಿಸಿದುದನ್ನೂ ದುಃಖಿತ ಕೌರವರು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಸುತ್ತ ಸೇರಿದುದನ್ನೂ ಸಂಜಯ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ನಾಯಕನಿಲ್ಲದೆ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಮುಂದುವರಿಯಲಾರದೆಂದು ಕೃಪ ಸಲಹೆ ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"संजय बताते हैं कि कर्ण के मरने पर कृप ने विलाप किया और शोकाकुल कौरव दुर्योधन के चारों ओर जुटे। कृप सलाह देते हैं कि बिना नेता के सेना आगे नहीं चल सकती।","te":"కర్ణుడు చనిపోయాక కృపుడు విలపించాడని, దుఃఖితులైన కౌరవులు దుర్యోధనుని చుట్టూ చేరారని సంజయుడు చెబుతాడు. నాయకుడు లేకుండా సేన కొనసాగలేదని కృపుడు సలహా ఇస్తాడు.","ta":"கர்ணன் கொல்லப்பட்டதும் கிருபர் புலம்பியதையும் துயருற்ற கௌரவர் துரியோதனனைச் சூழ்ந்ததையும் சஞ்சயன் கூறுகிறான். தலைவன் இன்றிப் படை தொடர முடியாது என்று கிருபர் அறிவுரைக்கிறார்.","ml":"കർണ്ണൻ കൊല്ലപ്പെട്ടശേഷം കൃപർ വിലപിച്ചതും, ദുഃഖിതരായ കൗരവർ ദുര്യോധനനു ചുറ്റും കൂടിയതും സഞ്ജയൻ പറയുന്നു. നേതാവില്ലാതെ സേനയ്ക്ക് മുന്നോട്ടുപോകാനാവില്ലെന്ന് കൃപർ ഉപദേശിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.3; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"शल्यपर्व","titleEn":"Shalya Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"शृणु राजन्नवहितो यथा वृत्तो महान्क्षयः ।\nकुरूणां पाण्डवानां च समासाद्य परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen attentively, king, to how the great destruction of the Kurus and Pandavas occurred when they met each other."}},{"n":2,"text":"निहते सूतपुत्रे तु पाण्डवेन महात्मना ।\nविद्रुतेषु च सैन्येषु समानीतेषु चासकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the charioteer's son had been killed by the great-souled Pandava, and the scattered troops were gathered again and again,"}},{"n":3,"text":"विमुखे तव पुत्रे तु शोकोपहतचेतसि ।\nभृशोद्विग्नेषु सैन्येषु दृष्ट्वा पार्थस्य विक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"when your son was turned away, his mind struck by grief, and the armies were greatly shaken seeing Arjuna's prowess,"}},{"n":4,"text":"ध्यायमानेषु सैन्येषु दुःखं प्राप्तेषु भारत ।\nबलानां मथ्यमानानां श्रुत्वा निनदमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"when the troops were brooding and sunk in sorrow, Bharata, hearing the mighty roar of the forces being crushed,"}},{"n":5,"text":"अभिज्ञानं नरेन्द्राणां विकृतं प्रेक्ष्य संयुगे ।\nपतितान्रथनीडांश्च रथांश्चापि महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"seeing the insignia of kings disfigured on the battlefield, the fallen chariot-seats and the chariots of great men,"}},{"n":6,"text":"रणे विनिहतान्नागान्दृष्ट्वा पत्तींश्च मारिष ।\nआयोधनं चातिघोरं रुद्रस्याक्रीडसंनिभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"seeing the elephants and foot-soldiers slain in the battle, sir, and the dreadful field like Rudra's playground,"}},{"n":7,"text":"अप्रख्यातिं गतानां तु राज्ञां शतसहस्रशः ।\nकृपाविष्टः कृपो राजन्वयःशीलसमन्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"seeing hundreds of thousands of kings reduced to nameless ruin, Kripa, filled with compassion, O king, endowed with age and good character,"}},{"n":8,"text":"अब्रवीत्तत्र तेजस्वी सोऽभिसृत्य जनाधिपम् ।\nदुर्योधनं मन्युवशाद्वचनं वचनक्षमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"that radiant man, skilled in speech, went up to the king in his anger and spoke these words to Duryodhana."}},{"n":9,"text":"दुर्योधन निबोधेदं यत्त्वा वक्ष्यामि कौरव ।\nश्रुत्वा कुरु महाराज यदि ते रोचतेऽनघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Duryodhana, listen to what I will say to you, Kaurava; having heard it, do it, great king, if it pleases you, blameless one.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"न युद्धधर्माच्छ्रेयान्वै पन्था राजेन्द्र विद्यते ।\nयं समाश्रित्य युध्यन्ते क्षत्रियाः क्षत्रियर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"King, there is no better path than the duty of war, relying on which Kshatriyas fight, best of Kshatriyas.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"पुत्रो भ्राता पिता चैव स्वस्रेयो मातुलस्तथा ।\nसंबन्धिबान्धवाश्चैव योध्या वै क्षत्रजीविना ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Son, brother, father, sister's son, maternal uncle, relatives by marriage and kinsmen: all these a man who lives by the warrior's trade must fight.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"वधे चैव परो धर्मस्तथाधर्मः पलायने ।\nते स्म घोरां समापन्ना जीविकां जीवितार्थिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In killing lies the highest duty, and in fleeing lies unrighteousness. We have fallen into this dreadful livelihood, desiring only to live.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"तत्र त्वां प्रतिवक्ष्यामि किंचिदेव हितं वचः ।\nहते भीष्मे च द्रोणे च कर्णे चैव महारथे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"On this I will tell you a word that is beneficial. Now that Bhishma, Drona and the great warrior Karna are slain,\""}},{"n":14,"text":"जयद्रथे च निहते तव भ्रातृषु चानघ ।\nलक्ष्मणे तव पुत्रे च किं शेषं पर्युपास्महे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Jayadratha slain, and your brothers, blameless one, and your son Lakshmana, what is left for us to rely on?\""}},{"n":15,"text":"येषु भारं समासज्य राज्ये मतिमकुर्महि ।\nते संत्यज्य तनूर्याताः शूरा ब्रह्मविदां गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Those upon whom we laid our burden and set our hopes on the kingdom, those heroes have cast off their bodies and gone to the goal of the knowers of Brahman.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"वयं त्विह विनाभूता गुणवद्भिर्महारथैः ।\nकृपणं वर्तयिष्याम पातयित्वा नृपान्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We, deprived of those excellent great warriors, will drag out a wretched life, having made many kings fall.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"सर्वैरपि च जीवद्भिर्बीभत्सुरपराजितः ।\nकृष्णनेत्रो महाबाहुर्देवैरपि दुरासदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Even if all of us were alive, the unconquered Arjuna, dark-eyed and mighty-armed, would be hard for even the gods to approach.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"इन्द्रकार्मुकवज्राभमिन्द्रकेतुमिवोच्छ्रितम् ।\nवानरं केतुमासाद्य संचचाल महाचमूः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The great army trembled when it met the monkey banner, towering like Indra's banner, bright as Indra's bow and thunderbolt.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"सिंहनादेन भीमस्य पाञ्चजन्यस्वनेन च ।\nगाण्डीवस्य च निर्घोषात्संहृष्यन्ति मनांसि नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Our minds are filled with dread at Bhima's lion roar, the sound of the Panchajanya conch and the twang of the Gandiva.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"चरन्तीव महाविद्युन्मुष्णन्ती नयनप्रभाम् ।\nअलातमिव चाविद्धं गाण्डीवं समदृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Gandiva was seen whirled like a firebrand, flashing like great lightning and stealing the brightness of the eyes.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"जाम्बूनदविचित्रं च धूयमानं महद्धनुः ।\nदृश्यते दिक्षु सर्वासु विद्युदभ्रघनेष्विव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The great bow, adorned with Jambunada gold, as it is brandished, is seen in all directions like lightning in thick clouds.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"उह्यमानश्च कृष्णेन वायुनेव बलाहकः ।\nतावकं तद्बलं राजन्नर्जुनोऽस्त्रविदां वरः ।\nगहनं शिशिरे कक्षं ददाहाग्निरिवोत्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Carried by Krishna as a cloud is carried by the wind, Arjuna, best of those who know weapons, burned your army, king, as a fire flares up and burns a thicket in the dry season.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"गाहमानमनीकानि महेन्द्रसदृशप्रभम् ।\nधनंजयमपश्याम चतुर्दन्तमिव द्विपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We saw Dhananjaya plunging into the ranks, with a radiance like Mahendra's, like a four-tusked elephant.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"विक्षोभयन्तं सेनां ते त्रासयन्तं च पार्थिवान् ।\nधनंजयमपश्याम नलिनीमिव कुञ्जरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We saw Dhananjaya shaking your army and terrifying the kings, like an elephant churning a lotus pond.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"त्रासयन्तं तथा योधान्धनुर्घोषेण पाण्डवम् ।\nभूय एनमपश्याम सिंहं मृगगणा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We saw the Pandava terrifying warriors with the sound of his bow, as herds of beasts see a lion.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"सर्वलोकमहेष्वासौ वृषभौ सर्वधन्विनाम् ।\nआमुक्तकवचौ कृष्णौ लोकमध्ये विरेजतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The two Krishnas, the great archers of all the world, the bulls among all bowmen, their armor fastened, shone in the midst of the world.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"अद्य सप्तदशाहानि वर्तमानस्य भारत ।\nसंग्रामस्यातिघोरस्य वध्यतां चाभितो युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seventeen days now, Bharata, this most dreadful war has gone on, with slaughter on every side.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"वायुनेव विधूतानि तवानीकानि सर्वशः ।\nशरदम्भोदजालानि व्यशीर्यन्त समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Your divisions, scattered everywhere as if by wind, have been dispersed all around like autumn clouds.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"तां नावमिव पर्यस्तां भ्रान्तवातां महार्णवे ।\nतव सेनां महाराज सव्यसाची व्यकम्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The son of Pritha, left-handed archer, shook your army like a ship tossed in a great ocean, spun by the wind.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"क्व नु ते सूतपुत्रोऽभूत्क्व नु द्रोणः सहानुगः ।\nअहं क्व च क्व चात्मा ते हार्दिक्यश्च तथा क्व नु ।\nदुःशासनश्च भ्राता ते भ्रातृभिः सहितः क्व नु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Where is the charioteer's son now, and where is Drona with his followers? Where am I, where are you yourself, and where is the Hardikya? Where is your brother Duhshasana with his brothers?\""}},{"n":31,"text":"बाणगोचरसंप्राप्तं प्रेक्ष्य चैव जयद्रथम् ।\nसंबन्धिनस्ते भ्रातॄंश्च सहायान्मातुलांस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seeing Jayadratha within the range of Arjuna's arrows, and your kinsmen, brothers, allies and uncles,\""}},{"n":32,"text":"सर्वान्विक्रम्य मिषतो लोकांश्चाक्रम्य मूर्धनि ।\nजयद्रथो हतो राजन्किं नु शेषमुपास्महे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Jayadratha was killed, O king, as Arjuna overpowered them all while they looked on and set his foot on the heads of the worlds; what do we now rely on?\""}},{"n":33,"text":"को वेह स पुमानस्ति यो विजेष्यति पाण्डवम् ।\nतस्य चास्त्राणि दिव्यानि विविधानि महात्मनः ।\nगाण्डीवस्य च निर्घोषो वीर्याणि हरते हि नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What man is there who will conquer the Pandava, whose many divine weapons and the twang of whose Gandiva take our strength away?\""}},{"n":34,"text":"नष्टचन्द्रा यथा रात्रिः सेनेयं हतनायका ।\nनागभग्नद्रुमा शुष्का नदीवाकुलतां गता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This army, its leaders slain, is like a night without a moon, like a dry river with trees broken by elephants, thrown into confusion.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"ध्वजिन्यां हतनेत्रायां यथेष्टं श्वेतवाहनः ।\nचरिष्यति महाबाहुः कक्षेऽग्निरिव संज्वलन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"With his army's leader eyes put out, the white-horsed mighty-armed one will roam as he wishes, blazing like fire in dry grass.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"सात्यकेश्चैव यो वेगो भीमसेनस्य चोभयोः ।\nदारयेत गिरीन्सर्वाञ्शोषयेत च सागरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The speed of Satyaki and of Bhimasena, both of them, could split all mountains and dry up the oceans.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"उवाच वाक्यं यद्भीमः सभामध्ये विशां पते ।\nकृतं तत्सकलं तेन भूयश्चैव करिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What Bhima said in the middle of the assembly, lord, he has fulfilled completely, and he will do so again.\""}},{"n":38,"text":"प्रमुखस्थे तदा कर्णे बलं पाण्डवरक्षितम् ।\nदुरासदं तथा गुप्तं गूढं गाण्डीवधन्वना ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When Karna stood at the front, the Pandava army was guarded, hard to approach, protected and hidden by the wielder of the Gandiva.\""}},{"n":39,"text":"युष्माभिस्तानि चीर्णानि यान्यसाधूनि साधुषु ।\nअकारणकृतान्येव तेषां वः फलमागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You have done to the good the things that are wrong, without reason; now their fruit has come to you.\""}},{"n":40,"text":"आत्मनोऽर्थे त्वया लोको यत्नतः सर्व आहृतः ।\nस ते संशयितस्तात आत्मा च भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For your own sake you strove to gather the whole world; now it is in danger, my son, and you yourself too, best of Bharatas.\""}},{"n":41,"text":"रक्ष दुर्योधनात्मानमात्मा सर्वस्य भाजनम् ।\nभिन्ने हि भाजने तात दिशो गच्छति तद्गतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Protect yourself, Duryodhana; the self is the vessel of everything. When the vessel is broken, what is in it scatters in all directions.\""}},{"n":42,"text":"हीयमानेन वै संधिः पर्येष्टव्यः समेन च ।\nविग्रहो वर्धमानेन नीतिरेषा बृहस्पतेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"One who is declining should seek peace, and one who is equal should too; war is for one who is growing. This is Brihaspati's policy.\""}},{"n":43,"text":"ते वयं पाण्डुपुत्रेभ्यो हीनाः स्वबलशक्तितः ।\nअत्र ते पाण्डवैः सार्धं संधिं मन्ये क्षमं प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We are weaker than the sons of Pandu in our strength, so I think peace with the Pandavas is fitting for you here, lord.\""}},{"n":44,"text":"न जानीते हि यः श्रेयः श्रेयसश्चावमन्यते ।\nस क्षिप्रं भ्रश्यते राज्यान्न च श्रेयोऽनुविन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"One who does not know what is good and scorns those who are better quickly falls from his kingdom and does not gain what is good.\""}},{"n":45,"text":"प्रणिपत्य हि राजानं राज्यं यदि लभेमहि ।\nश्रेयः स्यान्न तु मौढ्येन राजन्गन्तुं पराभवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If we can get the kingdom by bowing to the king, that would be good; but we should not walk into defeat through foolishness, king.\""}},{"n":46,"text":"वैचित्रवीर्यवचनात्कृपाशीलो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nविनियुञ्जीत राज्ये त्वां गोविन्दवचनेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"At the word of Vichitravirya's son and of Govinda, Yudhishthira, who is gentle by nature, would reinstate you in the kingdom.\""}},{"n":47,"text":"यद्ब्रूयाद्धि हृषीकेशो राजानमपराजितम् ।\nअर्जुनं भीमसेनं च सर्वं कुर्युरसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Whatever Hrishikesha says to the unconquered king, Arjuna and Bhimasena would doubtless do it all.\""}},{"n":48,"text":"नातिक्रमिष्यते कृष्णो वचनं कौरवस्य ह ।\nधृतराष्ट्रस्य मन्येऽहं नापि कृष्णस्य पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Krishna will not go against the word of the Kaurava, Dhritarashtra, and I think the Pandava will not go against Krishna's.\""}},{"n":49,"text":"एतत्क्षममहं मन्ये तव पार्थैरविग्रहम् ।\nन त्वा ब्रवीमि कार्पण्यान्न प्राणपरिरक्षणात् ।\nपथ्यं राजन्ब्रवीमि त्वां तत्परासुः स्मरिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I think this is proper for you: no war with the sons of Pritha. I do not say it from timidity or to save my life; I say what is good for you, king, and you will remember it when you are dying.\""}},{"n":50,"text":"इति वृद्धो विलप्यैतत्कृपः शारद्वतो वचः ।\nदीर्घमुष्णं च निःश्वस्य शुशोच च मुमोह च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having thus lamented, old Kripa, son of Sharadvat, sighing long and hot, grieved and was bewildered."}}]}]}